{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"FIRST 4-ARM CONCURRENT RUNS. Two plans (ts-carbon-dsx-card-web-component, scss-uswds-elements-dsx-token-migration) were reviewed by all four arms at the same time, on one ballot, judged in a single pass. The other nine Wave 3 runs ran three arms and added rebar afterwards through a separate supplementary panel. THE SCAFFOLDING CONFOUND IS ABSENT HERE: both plans were checked against rebar's real det_floor.DET_CHECKS and pass P1 readiness-shape, P5 task-dag, P8 reviewability, P10 verification-presence and P11 ac-vagueness on their own text, because both carry verbatim acceptance-criteria sections. So all four arms review byte-identical input. Only two things are supplied and neither alters plan text: the description cap raised via study config, and file_impact derived from paths the plan already names. The runner asserts no fitted file exists so scaffolding cannot silently return. JUDGE_INSTRUCTIONS_W4.md forks the W3 file with 49 lines changed; the evidence standard, deletion test and harm trap are byte-identical so classifications mean the same thing across all eleven runs. Ballot left unblinded to match the nine earlier runs, with explicit bias guards in both directions since rebar is the instrument under study."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789442995101511001,"uuid":"46bf3318-325a-4064-8a42-c2fecc330002"}